<figure class="dns-cache-layers" aria-labelledby="dns-cache-title">
  <figcaption id="dns-cache-title"><span class="content-kicker">Why one client stays stale</span><strong>The first cache with a live entry can answer before CoreDNS sees the query.</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="cache-stack">
    <article><span>01</span><b>Application / runtime</b><small>May cache independently of the OS</small><em>HIT? stop</em></article>
    <i aria-hidden="true">↓ miss</i>
    <article><span>02</span><b>OS / local resolver</b><small>Behavior varies by image and runtime</small><em>HIT? stop</em></article>
    <i aria-hidden="true">↓ miss</i>
    <article><span>03</span><b>NodeLocal DNSCache</b><small>Optional and isolated per Node</small><em>HIT? stop</em></article>
    <i aria-hidden="true">↓ miss</i>
    <article><span>04</span><b>CoreDNS</b><small>Positive and negative TTLs</small><em>HIT? stop</em></article>
    <i aria-hidden="true">↓ miss</i>
    <article><span>05</span><b>Upstream resolver</b><small>Only for forwarded names</small><em>answer</em></article>
  </div>
  <div class="cache-change"><span>Service fixed now</span><i aria-hidden="true">≠</i><span>Every cached answer changes now</span></div>
</figure>

